IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part V, Pilot Projects: sections 109 and 110.
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- Section 109 is a power of the Commission, with the approval of the Governor in Council, to make regulations establishing and
-- operating pilot projects; it is machinery and is marked `inert` in NOTES.md with its reason. Section 110 is not machinery: it
-- says when a regulation made under the Part stops having effect, which decides whether a pilot project's rules still apply to a
-- person. The pilot-project Regulations that exercise s 109 are the Regulations' Part IV (piece er5).
-- A date a regulation came into force is a fact, an input; this text fixes no such date.

§ `Section 110 - expiration of regulations`

-- "Regulations made under this Part that are not repealed cease to have effect three years after they come into force."
-- The third anniversary of the day they came into force is the first day they no longer have effect (`add years`, which clamps a
-- 29 February start to 28 February; fork F-ei3-25).
-- src:1802 | 110 Regulations made under this Part that are not repealed cease to have effect three years after they come into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 110 (src:1802)
GIVEN `the day on which the regulation came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 110 the day on which a regulation made under this Part ceases to have effect` IS
    `add years` `the day on which the regulation came into force` 3

-- A repealed regulation is outside the section (it says "that are not repealed"): NOTHING. Otherwise the regulation has ceased to
-- have effect on and after the third anniversary.
-- src:1802 | 110 Regulations made under this Part that are not repealed cease to have effect three years after they come into force.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 110 (src:1802)
GIVEN `the regulation made under this Part has been repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the regulation came into force` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 110 the regulation has ceased to have effect on the day` IS
    IF `the regulation made under this Part has been repealed`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the day in question` AT LEAST `s 110 the day on which a regulation made under this Part ceases to have effect` `the day on which the regulation came into force`)
